Template: homelab-database-ha/members
Type: string
Description: Cluster members as name:ip (comma-separated):
 Every Patroni member including this node, e.g.
 "pg01:10.0.0.1,pg02:10.0.0.2,pg03:10.0.0.3". For a single-node cluster
 just this host -- you can extend later by installing this package on the
 other members with the SAME list. Defaults to this host if left blank.

Template: homelab-database-ha/this_node
Type: string
Description: This node's name (must appear in the member list):
 Defaults to the short hostname.

Template: homelab-database-ha/vip
Type: string
Description: Database VIP, floated to the leader by keepalived (optional):
 Point pgbouncer and apps at this address so they follow the primary
 across failovers. Leave blank to skip keepalived (no VIP).

Template: homelab-database-ha/app_network
Type: string
Default: 10.50.0.0/22
Description: CIDR allowed to connect to the databases (pg_hba):
 The network your apps/pgbouncer connect from.

Template: homelab-database-ha/replication_password
Type: password
Description: Replication password (MUST be identical on every member):
 Leave blank to auto-generate -- only safe for a single-node cluster. For
 a multi-node cluster set the SAME value on every member (config is
 skipped with a warning if blank on a multi-node member).

Template: homelab-database-ha/wipe_existing
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Drop an existing PostgreSQL cluster so Patroni can create its own?
 DESTRUCTIVE. Only needed if this host already has a non-Patroni cluster at
 the data dir -- dump any data first. A fresh host needs this left false.
